{"kind":"event","event_id":4261,"event_uid":"01M2K3CY25WSE4MX75JDC04CV3","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":199,"issue_uid":"01M2K2MYH485Q5PYCE545P89SK","issue_short_id":"89sk","actor":"exam:1@run-148","hlc_physical_ms":1789494982725,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"2c287da870fb4697009dfe923601ead56012b0df8e2d3c9c702425139280e6aa","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2K3CY23CQ411TZZPVECG9PK","author":"exam:1@run-148","body":"Exam handed in: `fleet/tests/test_engine_coverage.mjs`, red at BASE for exactly one reason — `fleet/engine-coverage.mjs` does not exist, and leg (a)'s first assertion names it (the import is dynamic, so a missing module is an assertion and not a load-time crash).\n\nFour readings measured at BASE that the exam is written on, so a later session need not re-derive them:\n\n1. V8 answers the fixture engine `1` for the `a()` line, `0` for the line inside `if (false) { … }` and `0` for the `b()` line when only `a()` is called — the `if (false)` block DOES get a range of its own (count 0) nested inside `a`'s (count 1), so leg (j) is measurable. `export function b (n) {` itself counts 1 (the module range), so the changed line inside `b()` must be the body line, not the signature.\n2. Coverage IS still written when the sim calls `process.exit(1)` — that is what lets leg (d) ask for an exit code and a reading from the same run.\n3. Leg (c)'s copy is edited IDENTICALLY in the head commit, so at the instant the sim runs both files are byte-identical and the copy is exercised in full. That is the only arrangement under which a `url` matched by SUFFIX would mark the real file's `b()` line reached — which is the leg. Measured: with the copy's `a()` and `b()` both called, the real file's `b()` line still counts 0.\n4. `makeRepo` creates no subdirectory, so each scratch repo's `fleet/tests/` is made before the call; the rig's `stub` gets the clone cwd as its third argument and the implementer writes `fleet/run-engine.mjs` there.\n\nLegs (e)/(f) drive three `rig` runs (engine edited, `a.txt` edited, engine edited in a tree with no engine sims); leg (h) asks the third and fourth `Run:` lines in-process with the same range-then-match semantics. Leg (g) is the bridge's own second `Run:` line — a sim may not spawn `pytest` (`test_sims_are_hermetic` M4), so it is not encodable in the file; it is returned under `unsatisfiable` on that ground, not as a gap.\n\nValidated both ways before handing in: against a throwaway prototype of `engineCoverage` plus a prototype call site and the two doc rows the exam went GREEN end to end (last line `ALL TESTS PASSED`), and the prototype was then deleted — `git status` carries the exam alone and HEAD is still BASE. `node fleet/tests/test_sims_are_hermetic.mjs` sweeps the new file with 0 offenders (31 sims): the exam makes no spawn call of its own, names the fixture sims only in `fs` writes, and reads no absolute literal outside the checkout and `os.tmpdir()`.","created_at":"2026-09-15T17:56:22.723571885Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T17:56:22.725Z"}
